docker-php: applied to the ZTS build in Dockerfile (php-zts-builder stage).
Upstream fix proposed in https://github.com/php/php-src/pull/24516 (for https://github.com/php/php-src/issues/24492).
Remove once a PHP 8.5 release contains an upstream fix (the patch then fails to apply).

From ee62bc9dba693d109cb495b70eb288e3d527c1f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Metzler <richard@paadee.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:25:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ext/xml with Expat reaching the hard memory limit

The memory handling suite passed to Expat used the non-fallible
allocator, so a document making Expat allocate past memory_limit
killed the process at the hard memory limit instead of raising the
regular "Allowed memory size exhausted" error.

Expat handles allocation failures (XML_ERROR_NO_MEMORY), so use the
fallible allocator like the other converted third-party wrappers.

Fixes ext/xml/tests/oom_xml_parse_ns.phpt and ext/xml/tests/gh14637.phpt
when building with --with-expat.

See GH-24492.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ext/xml/xml.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/xml/xml.c b/ext/xml/xml.c
index a80f8ade6f..df4deac1c3 100644
--- a/ext/xml/xml.c
+++ b/ext/xml/xml.c
@@ -206,14 +206,16 @@ static PHP_GINIT_FUNCTION(xml)
 	xml_globals->default_encoding = (XML_Char*)"UTF-8";
 }
 
+/* Expat handles allocation failures (XML_ERROR_NO_MEMORY), so let it fail
+ * instead of exceeding the hard memory limit. */
 static void *php_xml_malloc_wrapper(size_t sz)
 {
-	return emalloc(sz);
+	return femalloc(sz, /* fallible */ true);
 }
 
 static void *php_xml_realloc_wrapper(void *ptr, size_t sz)
 {
-	return erealloc(ptr, sz);
+	return ferealloc(ptr, sz, /* fallible */ true);
 }
 
 static void php_xml_free_wrapper(void *ptr)
-- 
